                    <span>1</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 1" value="2" />
                    <span>2</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 1" value="3" />
                    <span>3</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 1" value="4" />
                    <span>4</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 1" value="5" />
                    <span>5</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 1" value="6" />
                    <span>6</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 1" value="7" />
                    <span>7</span>
                </label>
            </div>
            <p class="question-text">2. I use GenAI to explain difficult course concepts, theories, or formulas in simpler terms</p>
            <div class="answer">
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 2" value="True" />
                    <span>True</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 2" value="False" />
                    <span>False</span>
                </label>
            </div>
            <p class="question-text">3. I use GenAI to act as a practice partner or quize me on material before an exam.</p>
            <div class="answer">
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 3" value="True" />
                    <span>True</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 3" value="False" />
                    <span>False</span>
                </label>
            </div>
            <p class="question-text">4. I use GenAI to help outline, structure, or brainstorm ideas for my own original writing.</p>
            <div class="answer">
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 4" value="True" />
                    <span>True</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 4" value="False" />
                    <span>False</span>
                </label>
            </div>
            <p class="question-text">5. I use GenAI to generate full paragraphs, sections, or answers for my homework that I then submit with little to no modification.</p>
            <div class="answer">
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 5" value="Always" />
                    <span>Always</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 5" value="Sometimes" />
                    <span>Sometimes</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 5" value="Never" />
                    <span>Never</span>
                </label>
            </div>
            <p class="question-text">6. I use GenAI primarily to save time and finish assignments as quickly as possible rather than to understand the material.</p>
            <div class="answer">
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 6" value="Always" />
                    <span>Always</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 6" value="Sometimes" />
                    <span>Sometimes</span>
                </label>
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="GenAI Question 6" value="Never" />
                    <span>Never</span>
                </label>
            </div>
        </div>
        <button type="button" data-step="2">Previous</button>
        <button type="button" data-validate-step="4">Next: Self-Efficacy Scale</button>

    </form>
</section>

<script>
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-validate-step="4"]').forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
            const currentStep = document.getElementById('step3');
            const radioGroups = currentStep?.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[type="radio"]') ?? [];

            const groupNames = [...new Set(
                Array.from(radioGroups).map(radio => radio.name)
            )];

            const unanswered = groupNames.filter((groupName) => (
                !currentStep?.querySelector(`input[name="${groupName}"]:checked`)
            ));

            if (unanswered.length > 0) {
                alert('Please answer all questions.');
                return;
            }

            // GenAI is an intermediate scale: validate it here, then let the
            // final self-efficacy scale collect and submit the complete payload.
            const nextStep = document.getElementById('step4');
            if (currentStep && nextStep) {
                currentStep.classList.remove('active');
                currentStep.classList.add('hidden');
                nextStep.classList.remove('hidden');
                nextStep.classList.add('active');
            }
            window.scrollTo({
                top: 0,
                behavior: 'smooth'
            });
        });
    });
</script>

